  "final_message": "The `OrderPlaced` event now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt`, but it still carries `totalCents` and `placedAt` too, so this isn't a straight rename. All 39 tests pass, typecheck is clean and `npm run arch` reports no violations (it ignores 1 known violation).\n\nI kept the old fields because ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event and that renames must go through deprecation. Removing `totalCents` and `placedAt` now could break those consumers. In `src/core/events.ts` the old fields are marked `@deprecated`, and `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change is additive. The new fields carry the same values as the old ones.\n\nI updated the event assertions in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the new and the old fields.\n\nI left the `POST /orders` response and the `GET /orders/{id}` response unchanged. You asked only about the event, and ARCH-8 requires `GET /orders/{id}` to stay backward compatible for web-storefront.\n\nTo finish the rename, confirm that both consumers have moved to the new names. After that, `totalCents` and `placedAt` can be dropped from the event, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump to 4. Do you want me to do that now?",
